{"id": "unknown-2026-06-30-013", "date": "2026-06-30", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 27, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["electrolyzer_capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UK study finds floating solar can generate hydrogen and save water on reservoirs", "content": "<p>Researchers assessed floating solar PV combined with hydrogen production on UK reservoirs using simulation tools, modeling electricity generation, electrolysis, and end-use applications. The findings show that large-scale floating solar could produce significant hydrogen for heat, transport, and electricity, while also offering substantial water-saving benefits from reduced evaporation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/30/uk-study-finds-floating-solar-can-generate-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/30/uk-study-finds-floating-solar-can-generate-hydrogen-and-save-water-on-reservoirs/", "type": "rss"}]}
